acceptTest is test
acceptTest purpose "The squares sample is accepted and diagnosed as accepted; a record holding an enum declared below it, and a module with no main, are refused"
acceptTest verifies checkModule acceptsSubset
acceptTest verifies diagnose reportsFirstProblem
acceptTest verifies checkDeclarations rejectsOutsideDeclarations
acceptTest typeParameter none
acceptTest input none
acceptTest output none
acceptTest outputOwnedBy none
acceptTest raises none
acceptTest effect none
acceptTest uses none
acceptTest memoryHeap true
acceptTest async false
acceptTest maxRecursion none
acceptTest label begin loopKind none
acceptTest label begin within none
acceptTest label lexXDone loopKind none
acceptTest label lexXDone within none
acceptTest label groupXDone loopKind none
acceptTest label groupXDone within none
acceptTest label modelXDone loopKind none
acceptTest label modelXDone within none
acceptTest label acceptItDone loopKind none
acceptTest label acceptItDone within none
acceptTest label lexYDone loopKind none
acceptTest label lexYDone within none
acceptTest label groupYDone loopKind none
acceptTest label groupYDone within none
acceptTest label modelYDone loopKind none
acceptTest label modelYDone within none
acceptTest label noMainRefused loopKind none
acceptTest label noMainRefused within none
acceptTest label refused loopKind none
acceptTest label refused within none
acceptTest let source String "# A stage0 sample: an arithmetic loop. It prints the squares of 1 to `limit`\n# (1, 4, 9, 16, 25), one per line, from a `while` loop bounded by the module\n# constant `limit`, and exits with code 0.\n\nsquares is module\nsquares purpose \"Print the squares of the whole numbers from 1 to a limit\"\nsquares path squares\nsquares imports standard.console\nsquares imports standard.math\nsquares imports standard.compare\nsquares exports main\n\nstdoutWriter is capability\nstdoutWriter purpose \"Authority to write lines to standard output\"\nstdoutWriter grants write console.stdout none\n\nlimit is constant\nlimit purpose \"The last number whose square is printed\"\nlimit type Int64\nlimit value 5\n\nmain is operation\nmain purpose \"Print the square of each whole number from 1 to the limit\"\nmain invariant none\nmain typeParameter none\nmain input none\nmain output ExitCode\nmain outputOwnedBy none\nmain raises none\nmain effect write console.stdout\nmain uses stdoutWriter\nmain memoryHeap false\nmain async false\nmain maxRecursion none\nmain label begin loopKind none\nmain label begin within none\nmain label nextSquare note \"Each pass prints one square; the loop returns to its header once per number\"\nmain label nextSquare loopKind while\nmain label nextSquare within none\nmain label nextSquare maxIterations limit\nmain label printSquare loopKind none\nmain label printSquare within nextSquare\nmain label advance loopKind none\nmain label advance within nextSquare\nmain label finished loopKind none\nmain label finished within none\nmain label failed loopKind none\nmain label failed within none\nmain let number Int64 1 mutable\nmain let one Int64 1 immutable\nmain let okCode ExitCode 0 immutable\nmain let failCode ExitCode 1 immutable\nmain at begin goto nextSquare\nmain at nextSquare do pastLimitCheck\nmain at nextSquare branch if pastLimit goto finished else goto printSquare\nmain at printSquare do square\nmain at printSquare do printIt\nmain at printSquare branch ifError printIt goto failed else goto advance\nmain at advance do addOne\nmain at advance set number nextNumber\nmain at advance goto nextSquare\nmain at finished return ok okCode\nmain at failed return ok failCode\n\npastLimitCheck is call\npastLimitCheck in main\npastLimitCheck invokes compare.greaterThanInt64\npastLimitCheck argument left Int64 number copy\npastLimitCheck argument right Int64 limit copy\npastLimitCheck result pastLimit Bool\npastLimitCheck ownedBy none\npastLimitCheck cleanedBy none\npastLimitCheck borrows none\npastLimitCheck catch none\npastLimitCheck suppresses none\n\nsquare is call\nsquare in main\nsquare invokes math.multiplyInt64\nsquare argument left Int64 number copy\nsquare argument right Int64 number copy\nsquare result squared Int64\nsquare ownedBy none\nsquare cleanedBy none\nsquare borrows none\nsquare catch none\nsquare suppresses none\n\nprintIt is call\nprintIt in main\nprintIt invokes console.writeIntegerLine\nprintIt argument value Int64 squared copy\nprintIt result none\nprintIt ownedBy none\nprintIt cleanedBy none\nprintIt borrows none\nprintIt catch printError console.WriteError\nprintIt suppresses none\n\naddOne is call\naddOne in main\naddOne invokes math.addInt64\naddOne argument left Int64 number copy\naddOne argument right Int64 one copy\naddOne result nextNumber Int64\naddOne ownedBy none\naddOne cleanedBy none\naddOne borrows none\naddOne catch none\naddOne suppresses none\n" immutable
acceptTest let orderSource String "demo is module\ndemo path demo\ndemo imports none\ndemo exports main\n\nPoint is record\nPoint typeParameter none\nPoint field x Int64\nPoint field shape Shape\nPoint field label String\n\nShape is enum\nShape typeParameter none\nShape variant dot Int64\nShape variant empty none\n\nPoints is typeInstance\nPoints in none\nPoints instantiates list.List Point\n\nmain is operation\nmain input none\nmain output ExitCode\nmain raises none\n" immutable
acceptTest let orderExpected String "9:19: a record or enum holds only types declared above it (Shape)" immutable
acceptTest let noMainSource String "demo is module\ndemo path demo\n" immutable
acceptTest let noMainExpected String "1:1: the module has no main operation (demo)" immutable
acceptTest let refusedText String "the front end refused the source or a step failed" immutable
acceptTest let acceptedText String "accepted" immutable
acceptTest at begin do lexX
acceptTest at begin branch ifError lexX goto refused else goto lexXDone
acceptTest at lexXDone do newWordsX
acceptTest at lexXDone do newRowsX
acceptTest at lexXDone do groupX
acceptTest at lexXDone branch ifError groupX goto refused else goto groupXDone
acceptTest at groupXDone do newEntitiesX
